# android/ is tracked. The application id lives in it, and that id is the app's
# permanent identity on the Play Store — once published it cannot be changed
# without becoming a different app with no downloads and no reviews. Leaving
# the folder untracked meant the one irreversible decision in this repo was
# recorded nowhere, and a fresh clone would regenerate it from whatever --org
# the next person happened to type. Kiosk mode also lands here as hand-written
# Kotlin, which is the condition this comment used to describe.
#
# ios/ is not generated yet. Whoever adds it must pass the same
# --org io.github.zivanaa, or the two platforms become two different apps.
/ios/

# Secrets — never commit these
**/google-services.json
**/GoogleService-Info.plist
.env
*.jks
*.keystore

